# Which country drinks the most alcohol per adult?
subtitle: "Pick the country whose adults drink the most from four suspects, then see how France, Russia, Uganda and the world average compare."
tags: ["health","geography","data"]
format: quiz
thumb: "band \"Who drinks the most?\" note \"per adult\""

## Which country drinks the most alcohol per adult?
use: bar_chart
with:
    labels:
      - Saudi Arabia
      - World
      - France
      - Russia
      - Ireland
      - Uganda
      - Romania
    values:
      - 0
      - 5
      - 10
      - 11
      - 11
      - 11
      - 17
    value_labels: true
    ylim:
      - 0
      - 20
    y_label: Litres of pure alcohol per adult, 2020
    bar_colors: same
    icons:
      - {of: flag saudi arabia, set: twemoji}
      - {of: globe showing europe-africa, set: twemoji}
      - {of: flag france, set: twemoji}
      - {of: flag russia, set: twemoji}
      - {of: flag ireland, set: twemoji}
      - {of: flag uganda, set: twemoji}
      - {of: flag romania, set: twemoji}
    label_size: 34
sources:
    - id: owid_alc
      title: Alcohol consumption per person
      authors: Our World in Data, from the WHO Global Health Observatory via the World Bank
      year: 2026
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/total-alcohol-consumption-per-capita-litres-of-pure-alcohol
      finding: 'litres of pure alcohol per person aged 15+ in 2020: Romania 16.8 (the highest), Uganda 11.3, Ireland 10.8, Russia 10.5 (14.5 in 2005), France 10.3, world 4.9; near zero in Saudi Arabia, Kuwait, Pakistan and Bangladesh'

    icon f_france size 230 set twemoji x 140 y 360 icon_look picture of "flag france" hidden true
    text n_france "France" #2f2b26 x 140 y 205 font_size 52 hidden true
    icon f_russia size 230 set twemoji x 380 y 360 icon_look picture of "flag russia" hidden true
    text n_russia "Russia" #2f2b26 x 380 y 205 font_size 52 hidden true
    icon f_ireland size 230 set twemoji x 620 y 360 icon_look picture of "flag ireland" hidden true
    text n_ireland "Ireland" #2f2b26 x 620 y 205 font_size 52 hidden true
    icon f_romania size 230 set twemoji x 860 y 360 icon_look picture of "flag romania" hidden true
    text n_romania "Romania" #2f2b26 x 860 y 205 font_size 52 hidden true
    text clue "Clue: 17 litres" #b5482e cites ["owid_alc"] x 500 y 540 font_size 56 hidden true
    icon mug1 size 110 set twemoji x 560 y 580 icon_look picture of "beer mug" hidden true
    icon mug2 size 110 set twemoji x 650 y 580 icon_look picture of "beer mug" hidden true
    text beers "a day" #b5482e x 605 y 505 font_size 48 hidden true
    text times "3 × the world" #b5482e cites ["owid_alc"] x 620 y 590 font_size 46 hidden true

    card title "Who drinks the most?"

Which country drinks the most alcohol per adult? Four suspects: France, Russia, Ireland and Romania.
    draw f_france n_france f_russia n_russia f_ireland n_ireland f_romania n_romania

One clue: in the winner, the av (@draw clue@)erage adult gets through about seventeen litres of pure alcohol a year.

    ask "Tap the country you suspect." choose ["f_france","f_russia","f_ireland","f_romania"] answer f_romania reveal.text Romania! reveal.at.x 860 reveal.at.y 480 reveal.size 40
        right: Romania. The highest in the WHO's estimates, ahead of every wine, whisky and vodka nation.
        wrong: Look east of Paris, but well west of Moscow.

    erase f_france n_france f_russia n_russia f_ireland n_ireland f_romania n_romania clue

So the famous drinkers, France, Russia and Ireland, all sit around ten or eleven litres.
    draw axes bar_3 bar_4 bar_5

Romania stands well clear, at about seventeen.
    draw bar_7

That's about the alcohol in (@draw mug1 mug2 beers@) two large beers a day, for every adult, every day of the year.

    erase mug1 mug2 beers

    text rus "−27 % since 2005" above bar_4 gap 60 #2f6b8f cites ["owid_alc"] font_size 40

And Russia, home of the vodka cliché, has cut its drinking by more than a quarter since 2005.
    highlight bar_4

    erase rus

The surprise is Uganda: at about eleven litres, level with Russia and Ireland.
    draw bar_6

But the world as a whole? About five litres.
    draw bar_2

Because in much of the world, from Saudi Arabia to Bangladesh, the average is close to zero.
    draw bar_1

    draw times

So Romania's adults drink more than three times the world's average.
    highlight bar_7

